6. Assignment submission
Upload the link to your public GitHub repository to the assignment in the e-learning (Moodle). Every student submits, also when working in a pair.
The repository contains the code and the outputs of all tasks of this lab, a subfolder per task:

hello.py, AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md, PLAN.md, RUNS.md (parts 2–3);
the folders of your three tasks from part 4 with their outputs;
SPEC.md, the code, the saved results, the HTML report and the five slides of the ML study (part 5);
a short AI-use note in README.md: which agent and model you used and what you checked yourself.







NoteIf you finish early





Try PCA inside the cross-validation pipeline and explain what reducing two features to one loses; keep your final test result as it is and label the new run as an extra experiment. Or run two agents at once in separate Git worktrees: one on the report’s styling, one on the experiment code; merge only after checking both. Or recreate a second teacher demo.
